---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

import HomeImage from "@/assets/images/randp-home.png";
import AboutImage from "@/assets/images/randp-about.png";
import ServicesImage from "@/assets/images/randp-services.png";

import "@/assets/css/main.css";
---

<Layout>
  <main>
    <div class="wrap top">
      <a class="back" href="/projects">&larr; Back to all projects</a>
      <h1>R&amp;P Consulting</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        R&P Consulting is a Nairobi-based tax, accounting, and compliance firm.
        They needed a website that went beyond describing their services, one
        that could handle client bookings, onboard new team members without
        manual admin work, and meet Kenya's data protection requirements, all
        while being fast and well-structured enough to rank locally on Google.
      </p>
      <dl class="meta">
        <div>
          <dt>Client</dt>
          <dd>R&amp;P Consulting Limited</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>What I did</dt>
          <dd>
            Custom WordPress theme development, Scheme.org, SEO and cookie
            consent plugin development, deployment
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Year</dt>
          <dd>2026</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Live site</dt>
          <dd>
            <a
              href="https://randp-consulting.com"
              rel="noopener"
              target="_blank">Visit R&P Consulting</a
            >
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap">
      <figure class="shot wide">
        <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <div class="slot">
          <Image
            src={HomeImage}
            alt="R&P Consulting homepage"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <section>
        <div class="narrow body-copy">
          <h2>The problem</h2>
          <p>
            R&amp;P Consulting needed a platform that would become a working
            part of the business and not just another brochure website. This
            required onboarding that runs itself, a booking system clients
            actually want to use, and legal pages and cookie consent built
            around Kenya's Data Protection Act.
          </p>
          <p>
            They also needed to be found. Structured Schema.org data tells
            Google exactly who the firm is and what it offers, so local clients
            searching for tax, accounting, legal and HR help see R&amp;P first.
          </p>
          <p>
            The audience was business owners and individuals across Nairobi who
            need a trusted hand with KRA filings, eTIMS, payroll, HR, legal, and
            compliance. This site speaks to them directly.
          </p>
          <p>
            A theme builder or an off-the-shelf plugin stack couldn't get there
            without ending up slow, fragile, or non-compliant. So I built a
            custom classic wordpress theme from scratch.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>What I built</h2>
        <div class="feats">
          <div>
            <h3>A theme written from scratch</h3>
            <p>
              No page builder and no starter theme. Templates, custom post types
              for team members and services, and editable fields through ACF, so
              the firm updates content without touching code.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Built for local search</h3>
            <p>
              Implemented schema markup (AccountingService, Person, FAQPage,
              BreadcrumbList) sitewide and on individual templates, so search
              engines can correctly understand and surface the firm's services
              and team and that the firm's expertise is visible to Google.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Appointment Booking system</h3>
            <p>
              Integrated Simply Schedule Appointments with a custom popup modal,
              so clients can book consultations directly from the site without
              back-and-forth emails.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Automated Staff Onboarding</h3>
            <p>
              Built a custom Team Member post type with a save_post hook that
              automatically creates a linked WordPress user account whenever a
              new team member profile is published, removing several manual
              admin steps every time R&P hires.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Cookie consent and Data Protection Compliance</h3>
            <p>
              Built a custom cookie consent plugin and legal pages tailored
              specifically to Kenya's Data Protection Act (2019) not a generic
              GDPR template repurposed for a different jurisdiction. The plugin
              was designed to be reusable across future projects.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <h3>Fast, light front end</h3>
            <p>
              Tailwind CSS v4 compiled with Vite, with HTMX handling blog
              pagination so pages update without a full reload.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="pair">
          <figure class="shot half">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <div class="slot">
              <Image
                src={AboutImage}
                alt="R&P Consulting About page"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <figcaption>Team page with structured profile data.</figcaption>
            </div>
          </figure>

          <figure class="shot half">
            <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
            <div class="slot">
              <Image
                src={ServicesImage}
                alt="R&P Consulting Services page"
                loading="lazy"
              />
              <figcaption>Services built from a custom post type.</figcaption>
            </div>
          </figure>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="narrow body-copy process">
        <h2>How it's built</h2>
        <h3>Why a custom theme</h3>
        <p>
          A page builder plus a stack of plugins would have covered the basics,
          but not the combination R&amp;P needed, which was Kenya DPA-aware
          consent, structured data, a booking flow, and fast pages. Every layer
          in a builder stack adds markup, scripts, and another thing to update.
        </p>
        <p>
          A purpose-built PHP theme ships only what the site uses, and nothing
          in it depends on a vendor's roadmap. Plugins are limited to the jobs
          where a mature one is the simpler answer. Scheduling uses Simply
          Schedule Appointments, and TGMPA makes sure the required ones are
          installed.
        </p>

        <h3>Asset pipeline</h3>
        <p>
          CSS and JavaScript are bundled with Vite. Styling is Tailwind CSS v4,
          with the brand's colours and type scale defined as <code>@theme</code> tokens
          so the design lives in one place. Fonts are self-hosted, and icons are self-hosted
          SVGs served through a small <code>randp_icon()</code> helper rather than
          an icon CDN.
        </p>
        <p>
          That means no third-party requests for core assets and no
          render-blocking calls to external hosts. Interactivity is kept
          deliberately light since the build Alpine.js for small UI behaviour,
          and HTMX for blog category filtering and pagination, which swaps in
          server-rendered HTML instead of shipping a client-side app.
        </p>

        <h3>Content structure</h3>
        <p>
          Content is modelled as custom post types, with ACF fields and custom
          metaboxes for repeater-style data. Team members and services are their
          own types, so the client edits structured fields instead of laying out
          pages.
        </p>
        <p>
          Creating a team member automatically creates a linked WordPress user,
          which removes a manual onboarding step. Each team profile is also the
          source for its own Person markup, which supports the firm's
          credibility signals in search.
        </p>
        <p>
          Structured data is generated from that same content. The site
          implements Organization, AccountingService, Person, FAQPage, and
          Article schema, plus Open Graph tags. Nothing is hand-pasted into
          pages, so the markup stays in sync when the content changes.
        </p>

        <h3>Privacy and compliance</h3>
        <p>
          Cookie consent is a bespoke plugin built around Kenya's Data
          Protection Act rather than a generic banner. It is kept as a plugin
          rather than part of the theme so it survives a redesign.
        </p>

        <h3>Security and deployment</h3>
        <p>The site sits behind Cloudflare for CDN and WAF.</p>
        <p>
          Releases are packaged and pushed to a staging environment with rsync,
          so the client can review changes before anything touches production.
        </p>
        <p>
          The move to production followed a fixed runbook: full backup, WP-CLI
          search-replace (skipping GUID columns to keep serialized data intact),
          DNS cutover, then decommissioning staging.
        </p>
        <ul class="tags">
          <li>PHP</li>
          <li>WordPress</li>
          <li>Tailwind CSS v4</li>
          <li>Vite</li>
          <li>Alpine.js</li>
          <li>HTMX</li>
          <li>ACF</li>
          <li>WP-CLI</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2>Results</h2>
        <div class="results">
          <div class="res">
            <strong>Sub 2 seconds</strong><span>Load time</span>
          </div>
          <div class="res">
            <strong>~3000</strong><span>Visitors per month</span>
          </div>
          <div class="res">
            <strong>Live since</strong><span>August 2026</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <blockquote>
          Fantastic work by Kennedy. He built us a platforn that incorporated
          all the functions we needed and gave us a presence on Google. Now, we
          are proud to share our domain name with clients instead of the
          company's social media profiles.<cite
            >Puritie. R, Managing Partner, R&amp;P Consulting</cite
          >
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="band">
      <div class="wrap next">
        <a class="proj" href="/projects/pos-system"
          ><small>Next project</small><span class="t">Retail point of sale</span
          ></a
        >
        <a class="btn ghost" href="/projects">View all work</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="contact">
      <div class="wrap cta">
        <h2>Need a similar website, platform or tool for your business?</h2>
        <p>Tell me what you're building and I'll reply with next steps.</p>
        <a
          class="btn"
          href="mailto:kengitahi@proton.me?subject=Project%20enquiry"
          >Start a project</a
        >
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
